And for this one...

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.400
It's taking up nutrients for a...

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.500
nearby blood vessel.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.600
Then you come back over to the other document so this is where it's helpful to

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.200
have yourself split screens so this can be on one side and the document can be on the other.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.200
and then based on what you saw.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.300
in that

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.246
little interactive, you answer these questions.

00:01:08.246 --> 00:01:11.598
So you can see this first one was for muscle cell, and these are the answers.

00:01:11.598 --> 00:01:14.559
If you get one wrong, it will tell you, hey, this one's not correct,

00:01:14.559 --> 00:01:16.300
but these are the ones that are correct.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.900
Okay. And then you go to the next one. So photo receptor, cancer, and so on.
